## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Create a meeting, set it active, and generate a summary
  desc: The core meeting round-trip — create against a call channel, make it the active meeting, generate an AI summary.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-1.3, F-1.4, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-4.1, F-4.2, T-1, T-2, T-5]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - channel: a call Channel object exists in that space (plugin-calls) — meeting creation requires either a channel or an event anchor
    - plugin-meeting is enabled — it is OFF by default outside `isDev`/local dev builds (see `getDefaults` in `plugin-defs.tsx`, which only lists it under the `isDev` block)
    - no Meeting named "QA Meeting" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the meeting
      do: In the call's MeetingsList panel, click "Create Meeting" and name it "QA Meeting".
      invoke: [op:Create] { name: "QA Meeting", channel: $given.channel }
      capture: created
      expect: a Meeting named "QA Meeting" is returned, linked to an empty Transcript, notes Text, and summary Text
      assert: return !!$created.object && !!$created.object.transcript && !!$created.object.notes;
    - name: Set it active
      do: (the MeetingsList "Create Meeting" action does this automatically; selecting a row from the list does the same for an existing meeting)
      invoke: [op:SetActive] { object: $created.object }
      capture: active
      expect: MeetingArticle opens for "QA Meeting" and the call layer's activity payload carries its DXN
      assert: return $active.object?.id === $created.object.id;
      note: Coalesced with the previous step — `created.object` is live and cannot cross a snippet boundary.
    - name: Generate the summary
      do: In MeetingArticle, click "Generate Summary".
      invoke: [op:Summarize] { meeting: $created.object }
      expect: meeting.summary.content is non-empty and differs from its pre-invoke value
      assert: return (await $created.object.summary.load()).content.trim().length > 0;
      note: |
        Calls a live AI model (claude-3-5-haiku-latest) — non-deterministic output and real
        inference cost/latency. Meaningful content requires the meeting's transcript or notes to
        be non-empty first; against the empty fixture this test creates on its own, prime notes
        with a sentence before this step, or expect a thin/near-empty summary rather than an
        error.
  after:
    - name: Delete the meeting
      do: Right-click "QA Meeting" in the navtree (or its MeetingsList row) and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.space }
      expect: the meeting leaves the MeetingsList and any open plank closes
```

```mdl
test QA-2: A four-person meeting call, with notes taken during it
  desc: |
    The local user joins a Meeting's call after three colleagues have started, is greeted, they talk, and the local user
    writes the action items into the meeting's notes. The colleagues are simulated participants
    (plugin-calls `SetSimulatedParticipants`) played from pre-recorded avatar videos, and the
    local camera and microphone are a fourth video, so the test needs no camera and no EDGE. The
    seam also carries the script's lines, which stand in for live transcription.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, T-1]
  status: passing             # 2026-10-17, recorded by autocue/four-person-call.mjs with Higgsfield characters voiced by HeyGen, light mode; outline and transcript entry on each line's speaker
  given:
    - an identity exists, with display name "Astrid Holm"
    - space: the Alien Labs sample space (plugin-debug template) is open
    - plugin-calls and plugin-meeting are enabled — both default ON only in dev builds
    - the runtime config names an EDGE calls endpoint (the Call tab and Join need one configured,
      not reachable)
    - tracks: one equal-length WebM per participant (astrid, lucia, ben, tomas), made by
      `.agents/skills/autocue/scripts/conversation.mjs` from
      `autocue/fieldstone-dashboard.conversation.json`; the browser's camera and microphone play
      astrid's (`fake-media.mjs`), and the other three are served to the page, with
      `lucia-screen.webm` (the screen Lucía shares); its `timeline.json` gives each line's speaker
      id, start and text, and the screenshare's start
    - transcript: `timeline.json`'s `lines` as `{ speaker, start, text }`, each `speaker` id mapped to the
      participant's display name (`four-person-call.mjs` does this)
    - screen: `{ src: <lucia-screen.webm URL>, start: <timeline.json screenshares[0].start> }`
  steps:
    - name: Create and open the meeting
      do: Create a Meeting named "Cairn dashboard plugin: scoping" in the space and open it.
      invoke: [op:Create] { name: "Cairn dashboard plugin: scoping", db: $given.space.db }
      capture: created
      expect: MeetingArticle opens with the Notes, Transcript, Summary and Call tabs
    - name: Make the meeting active
      do: (no UI — test seam) Make the new meeting the active one, so the call's lines reach its transcript.
      invoke: [op:SetActive] { object: $created }
      expect: nothing visible
    - name: Add the colleagues
      do: (no UI — test seam) Fill the call with Lucía Ferreira, Ben Achterberg and Tomás Vidal, with Lucía's screenshare and the script's timed lines.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.calls.setSimulatedParticipants { participants: [{ name: "Lucía Ferreira", src: $given.tracks.lucia, screenshare: $given.screen }, { name: "Ben Achterberg", src: $given.tracks.ben }, { name: "Tomás Vidal", src: $given.tracks.tomas }], transcript: $given.transcript }
      expect: nothing visible yet — the participants appear on join
    - name: Join with camera and microphone on
      do: Open the Call tab, turn the camera on, unmute, and click Join.
      expect: |
        the grid shows four tiles named Astrid Holm, Lucía Ferreira, Ben Achterberg and Tomás Vidal,
        each playing its video; the toolbar's participant count reads 4
    - name: Open the transcript beside the call
      do: Open the companion side-by-side, choose the meeting companion, then its Transcript tab.
      expect: the call stays in the plank and the meeting's transcript shows in the companion
    - name: Greeted on arrival
      do: Watch the first seconds after joining.
      expect: |
        the local tile waves, Ben and Tomás acknowledge it (a small wave, a nod), and Lucía says
        "Hi. We just got started."
    - name: Lucía shares her screen
      do: When Lucía's screenshare tile appears, a couple of seconds into her opening line, click its expand button.
      expect: |
        the shared DXOS Architecture "Plugin metrics" sheet fills the call view, and its chart switches from
        horizontal to vertical bars as Lucía edits it
    - name: The conversation runs
      do: Watch the call until the last line ("… Thanks, everyone.").
      expect: |
        each speaker's tile shows the speaking outline while they talk and only then, in the
        script's order: Lucía, Lucía, Ben, Tomás, Lucía, Ben, Tomás, Lucía; each line appears
        once in the transcript, under its speaker's name, as it starts
      note: |
        Remote speaking state comes from each simulated participant's own audio, as a real
        participant's comes from their microphone; the local tile's comes from the fake microphone.
    - name: Write the action items
      do: Open the companion's Notes tab and type the three action items Lucía names.
      expect: the notes hold "Ben: share the sketch", "Tomás: build the plank", "Lucía: check it with Okapi"
    - name: Leave
      do: Click Leave.
      expect: the call returns to the lobby and the simulated participants leave the grid
  after:
    - name: Remove the simulated participants and the meeting
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.calls.setSimulatedParticipants { participants: [] }
      expect: the call manager has no simulated participants

test QA-3: Two people meet in one Meeting's call, with live transcription
  desc: |
    Alice and Bob, each with their own identity, share a space and open the same Meeting. Both join its call over
    RealtimeKit, each sees and hears the other, Alice turns transcription on, they talk, and the transcript fills in on
    both screens. Each person's camera and microphone play a pre-recorded track, so the test needs no camera, but it
    needs a real EDGE and RealtimeKit: this is the test that the call's media and transcript cross between two devices.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-3.2, F-3.6, T-1]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - two identities on separate devices (browser contexts), with display names "Alice" and "Bob"
    - space: "Launch sync", created by Alice; Bob has joined it by invitation
    - plugin-calls and plugin-meeting are enabled on both
    - the runtime config names an EDGE that serves `/calls/rooms/join`, and its RealtimeKit preset allows transcription
    - tracks: `alice.webm` and `bob.webm` of equal length, made by `autocue/two-peer-tracks.py`; each device's camera
      and microphone play its own (`fake-media.mjs`), and `timeline.json` gives each line's speaker, start and text
    - meeting: a Meeting named "Meetings plugin launch" in the space, open and active on both devices
  steps:
    - name: Open the call
      do: On both devices, open the Call tab, turn the camera on and unmute.
      expect: each shows its own camera preview and a Join button
    - name: Alice joins
      do: On Alice's device, click Join.
      expect: Alice's grid shows her own tile, and the toolbar offers Leave
    - name: Bob joins
      do: On Bob's device, click Join.
      expect: each grid shows two tiles, Alice and Bob, and each plays the other's video
    - name: Start transcription
      do: On Alice's device, choose Start transcription; on both, open the meeting companion's Transcript tab.
      expect: the transcript tab is open beside the call on both devices
    - name: They talk
      do: Start both tracks on one cue and watch until the last line ("Perfect. I'll put that in the meeting notes.").
      expect: |
        each line appears in both transcripts, attributed to its speaker, among them Bob's "I can have the release
        notes ready by Friday."
      note: Each device writes only its own speaker's segments, so a line reaches the other device through the space.
    - name: Bob leaves
      do: On Bob's device, click Leave.
      expect: Bob's call returns to the lobby, and Bob's tile leaves Alice's grid
```

