## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: In QA-2 the local user joins after the others have started and waves; the colleagues acknowledge it, and the leader says "Hi. We just got started."
  date: 2026-10-18
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [QA-2]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14040
```

```mdl
decision D-2: In QA-2 the leader shares the DXOS Architecture "Plugin metrics" sheet, which is maximised with the call view's expand control, and edits its chart to switch off horizontal bars.
  date: 2026-10-19
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [QA-2]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14040
```

```mdl
decision D-3: A simulated call's scripted lines are written to the active meeting's transcript as live transcription would write them. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [QA-2]
  why: Without live transcription in a simulated call, the transcript would stay empty and QA-2 could not check it.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14040
```

```mdl
decision D-4: QA-2 makes the meeting active before adding the colleagues, and binds the seam's transcript to the script's lines under display names, with the leader's screenshare. Fills in [D-2] and [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [QA-2]
  why: An agent runs QA-2's invoke literally, so it must match the operation's input and the active meeting.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14040
```

```mdl
decision D-5: A call's transcript comes from RealtimeKit's native transcription instead of each client recording its microphone: each participant writes its own segments to the linked Transcript feed, enriched with entity extraction, and the transcription toggle is meeting-wide.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-3, F-3.1, F-3.2, F-3.4, T-4, T-7, MeetingState]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/12046
```

```mdl
decision D-6: A meeting payload without `transcriptionEnabled` leaves transcription as it is, and SetActive does not re-announce the meeting the call already advertises. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-2.2, F-3.3]
  why: The meeting activity is one last-write-wins value, so a bare meeting selection would otherwise switch transcription off for everyone.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/12046
```

```mdl
decision D-7: A meeting payload without `transcriptDxn` unbinds the call's transcript feed and leaves the transcription toggle as it is. Fills in [D-6].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-3.5]
  why: Selecting another meeting mid-call publishes only its id, and the previous meeting's feed would otherwise keep receiving segments.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14179
```

```mdl
decision D-8: QA-3 tests a two-person Meeting call across two devices over RealtimeKit, with a real EDGE, each device's camera and microphone playing its own pre-recorded track, and the transcript checked on both.
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [QA-3]
  why: QA-2's colleagues are simulated on one device, so no test covered media and transcript crossing between two devices.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14186
```

```mdl
decision D-9: A Meeting's own call offers the Start/Stop transcription toggle on the meeting's toolbar while the user is in it. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-3.6, QA-3]
  why: The toggle existed only on channel calls, so a call started from a Meeting's Call tab could not turn transcription on; QA-3 found it.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14186
```

```mdl
decision D-10: The meeting's transcription toggle sits in MeetingArticle's own toolbar, and both toggles (channel call and meeting) share op:SetTranscription. Fills in [D-9].
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-3.6, MeetingArticle, SetTranscription]
  why: MeetingArticle builds its own toolbar, so an action on the meeting's graph node showed only in the plank heading's menu, where QA-3 could not find it.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14186
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap        # name[?]: TypeExpr  (# inline comment)
    literals?: UnionList     # a | b | c
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self              # feat blocks may contain feat blocks
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap            # external inputs (immutable inside component)
    state?: FieldMap            # internal reactive state
    slots?: FieldMap            # named ReactNode injection points
    actions?: ActionMap         # methods the component exposes or handles
    emits?: EventMap            # events the component raises to its parent
    layout?: CodeBlock          # ASCII sketch of visual structure (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap            # named input parameters
    output?: TypeExpr           # return type
    errors?: ErrorMap           # name: Prose  (when this error occurs)
    effects?: EffectList        # echo:read | echo:write | http | fs | ai:inference | calls:activity
    requires?: ServiceList      # injected service dependencies
    note?: Prose                # implementation guidance (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext decision
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0
  desc: |
    One decision about the spec, attributed to exactly one actor. The inline prose is the decision
    itself, stated as what is now true, not as the edit that was made.
  fields:
    date: Date                  # YYYY-MM-DD, the day the decision was made
    by: ActorRef                # user:<handle> | agent:<name> — the decider
    for?: UserRef               # agent entries only: the person the agent acted for
    affects?: RefList           # block ids the decision constrains
    supersedes?: Identifier     # an earlier decision this one replaces
    why?: Prose                 # the reason; on a user entry, only a reason the person gave
    rejected?: ProseList        # alternatives considered and why they lost
    source?: URI                # PR, review comment, issue, or session where it was made
  inline-prose: true
```
